Supported foreign formats
description: what yamlover overlays besides its own - each format, its renderer, and its limits
- >
  Yamlover overlays a directory tree, and a tree holds more than `.yo` files. Every foreign
  file is a first-class **node**: its format is inferred from the extension, its bytes stream
  from `/api/blob`, and a dedicated renderer shows it in place - as a page of its own and,
  where it fits, inline in a chapter as a body element. What yamlover does NOT do is pretend
  to own a foreign format's internals: each subchapter below states exactly how far the
  integration goes.
- >
  [Markdown](*:markdown) and [AsciiDoc](*:asciidoc) come first - the closest relatives of
  [marklower](*::documents:marklower), with an explicit boundary treaty. The rest are grouped
  by kin.
- *: markdown
- *: asciidoc
- *: plaintext
- *: latex
- *: plantuml
- *: html
- *: csv
- *: office
- *: books
- *: images
- *: media
- *: maps
